From: picture-frame build
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: switch the role even if the session is already valid

The role switch only forces the controller into the new mode if it had
to change the A or B session override. On the frame, VBUS of the USB-C
port is the power input, so the PHY reports both sessions as valid: the
override helpers return -EALREADY, the mode is never forced, and writing
"host" to the role switch leaves the controller in device mode.

Force the mode also when the controller is not in the requested mode.
dwc2_force_mode() can be called again for the current mode.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/drd.c
@@ -156,7 +156,13 @@
 
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hsotg->lock, flags);
 
-	if (!already && hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG)
+	/*
+	 * A session that is already valid does not mean that the controller
+	 * is in the requested mode: with VBUS present on the port, both the A
+	 * and the B session are valid, whatever the role.
+	 */
+	if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG &&
+	    (!already || dwc2_is_host_mode(hsotg) != (role == USB_ROLE_HOST)))
 		/* This will raise a Connector ID Status Change Interrupt */
 		dwc2_force_mode(hsotg, role == USB_ROLE_HOST);
 
